xemplifies the artistic expression of early human cultures and is associated with the Upper Paleolithic period, which marked a significant phase in human creativity and social development. The sculpture is an embodiment of fertility and femininity, reflecting the values and beliefs of its creators, who inhabited a world primarily defined by survival and subsistence.

